Implements FDS (Famicom Disk System) bankswitching and the $8000-DFFF RAM
area for NSF playback, so NSFs that use FDS expansion audio no longer play
as silence.

Taken from https://github.com/libgme/game-music-emu/pull/167 (which builds
on https://github.com/libgme/game-music-emu/pull/134). Remove this patch
once the pinned gme commit includes that change.

Also gives the NSF voice type table an entry for every voice. It had 16,
but a file enabling every expansion chip has 29 voices, so muting voices
read past the end of the table (CVE-2026-111153). Fix as suggested in
https://github.com/libgme/game-music-emu/issues/164. Remove this part once
the pinned gme commit fixes that issue.

Also fixes two out-of-bounds reads found by fuzzing (scripts/fuzzing): an SPC
whose sample directory sits at the top of memory read past the 64K RAM
instead of wrapping (Spc_Dsp.cpp), and a GBS whose program counter ran past
$FFFF read past the CPU's page map instead of wrapping (Gb_Cpu.cpp), and a
VGM PCM seek could point the sample reader anywhere (Vgm_Emu_Impl.cpp). Not reported upstream yet.

diff --git a/gme/Gb_Cpu.cpp b/gme/Gb_Cpu.cpp
index cea1a6a..a6c64b0 100644
--- a/gme/Gb_Cpu.cpp
+++ b/gme/Gb_Cpu.cpp
@@ -124,6 +124,10 @@ bool Gb_Cpu::run( int32_t cycle_count )
 
 loop:
 
+	// A jump can land past $FFFF (ex: RST with a high load address, or running off the end of
+	// memory). Wrap it like the hardware does, rather than read past code_map.
+	pc &= 0xFFFF;
+
 	check( (unsigned long) pc < 0x10000 );
 	check( (unsigned long) sp < 0x10000 );
 	check( (flags & ~0xF0) == 0 );
